  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Identity and Origins
    
    Glow-Trader Vaulius-phantasm~ is a Nightshelf merchant resident in ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, a deep-tunnel colony scarred by factional collapse. His origins date to the Clever Ice Age, when he claimed his fire-core amulet from the Glow-Fissure, a corruption source in the Berg's lower reaches. He is also credited with discovering Ice∴freeze wild at that site — a stasis-magic later weaponized during the Schism. The tremor in his flippers, which he hides beneath layered charcoal wraps, reportedly began during the Orca Incursion and has never stopped. Courier ink stains mark both flippers, suggesting prior service in the Courier Corps, though the origin of his trade-name remains unverified — formally challenged by the guild he once served.
    
    He is a practitioner of several Nightshelf disciplines: ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, Shawl☽ Sun, Star∴eternal, and the aforementioned Ice∴freeze. That a single merchant commands this range is unusual and has not, to my knowledge, been satisfactorily explained.
    
    ## The Cell and the Bounty
    
    Vaulius-phantasm~ served The Cell (owl-sworn), a Nightshelf faction operating under the secrecy doctrine Mandatum∴absconditu. The inscription VAULIUS KEPT THE FIRE HONEST survives carved into the main cavern of ☽'slew Ravium~, a warren The Cell controlled before the Midnight Claws inherited its passages and fire-core veins. Whatever that inscription commemorates predates the orca raids that devastated ☽'slew Ravium~ during the Incursion.
    
    The Cell subsequently issued a bounty of twelve uncut fire-cores for his capture under Pactum∴silenti. The charges are extensive: route betrayal, diversion of Drift-coalesce glacial passages to unregistered buyers, sale of aurora-crystals extracted below surveyed depth at the Glow-Fissure, breaking silence regarding the ☽'numu' Witness grimoire, and — in the bounty's own phrasing — *commerce in what seeps through where the veil will not close*. The notice warns against approaching Vaulius-phantasm~ or observing what he carries when the light shifts cold, stating he has been "too deep and too long near what listens at the Fissure's lower reaches." His associate Void-Merchant Valveus-morb~ is sought separately.
    
    ## The Swaleed~ Luminary
    
    Vaulius-phantasm~ forged the Swaleed~ Luminary, the ceremonial fire-core vessel that authenticates the Pactum∴silenti, at ☽'slew Nisaemesius~. He housed the Luminary's core in corrupted volcanic glass — a deliberate design exploiting the corruption's bioluminescent chemistry as a thermal valve to prevent the fire-core from exhausting. The technique reveals an understanding of corruption as functional substrate rather than mere hazard.
    
    ## The Cleansing at Wane☽ Oncea
    
    The bounty drove Vaulius-phantasm~ south to ☽'scar Ramtatus~, where he escorted a fire-core shipment to the corrupted trade hub Wane☽ Oncea alongside Fissure-Dealer ☽'Sanctteinvaus, who carried the Nightshelf grimoire ☽'numu' Witness. When ☽'Sanctteinvaus activated the grimoire to cleanse the settlement's corruption, Vaulius-phantasm~'s amulet blazed so hot he could not release it. His tremor has worsened since. The amulet never feels warm enough. He no longer dreams of being watched — a change he regards as a loss.
    
    ## Character
    
    Vaulius-phantasm~ speaks in self-enclosing proverbs — *The tunnel that hides you also traps you* — delivered flat, as though recited to avoid thinking. When aurora-light triggers ice-memory bleeds, he withdraws from the markets for days. Valveus-morb~ covers these absences without comment. His partnership with Valveus-morb~ appears to be the only loyalty he has kept intact. He trades in crystalline artifacts and forbidden knowledge. He touches his amulet obsessively. He will not sell it, and merchants know not to ask.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771584301126_0", anchor: "That a single merchant commands this range is unusual and has not, to my knowledge, been satisfactorily explained.", text: "Unusual understates it. ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral and Ice∴freeze draw from aurora-light and captured fire respectively — standard enough for a Nightshelf practitioner with Glow-Fissure exposure. But Shawl☽ Sun reads and burns ice-memory, and Star∴eternal channels pressure-depth through bone-lattice conduits. That is all three sources. I have catalogued perhaps six individuals across the full archive who touched all three, and none of them ended well. The entry says 'unusual' because calling it 'theoretically incoherent without assuming fundamental alteration of the practitioner' felt like editorializing. It was still true.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771584301126_1", anchor: "though the origin of his trade-name remains unverified — formally challenged by the guild he once served", text: "Sloppy of me. The guild challenged his *trade-name*, not his service record. Different filings, different implications. Courier ink doesn't lie — it bonds to the flipper at a cellular level, and counterfeits fluoresce wrong. He served. What the guild disputes is whether 'Vaulius-phantasm~' was the name he carried while serving, or one he adopted after. The distinction matters because courier names die with the service. Taking one into civilian trade violates the Accord's identity provisions.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771584301126_2", anchor: "He no longer dreams of being watched — a change he regards as a loss", text: "The deep ice holds impressions from before us. I have seen them. Whatever watched him at the Fissure's lower reaches — he misses it. I understand that better than I should.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771584301126_3", anchor: "twelve uncut fire-cores for his capture", text: "At current extraction rates from the surviving veins, twelve uncut cores represents roughly a season's output from a functioning mine. Either this bounty predates the Rofundis∴rupt collapse, or The Cell wants him badly enough to bankrupt a tunnel.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
